TITLE:: CompressorHistoryView
summary:: the last few seconds of level and gain change
categories:: Libraries>Compressor
related:: Classes/Compressor, Classes/CompressorPanel, Classes/CompressorCurveView

DESCRIPTION::
The input filled and dim, the output as a line over it, and the gain change
hanging from the top on a scale of its own that grows to fit the most it has
done - what a compressor's display has looked like since the hardware ones, and
still the quickest way to see whether the attack is catching the transients. It
listens to the compressor's code::\levels:: and keeps a ring of them. Click to
clear.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: comp
ARGUMENT:: parent
ARGUMENT:: bounds

METHOD:: seconds
How long the ring is. 8.

METHOD:: floorDb
METHOD:: grScaleMin
The gain change axis never shows less than this. 6.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: comp
METHOD:: view
METHOD:: refresh
METHOD:: remove
Stops listening.
